  "text" : "An attention score is just a dot product between one token's query and another token's key.\nEvery token starts as a vector.\nA learned matrix, WQ, moves each one into a query, which is the question this token\nasks.\nAnother matrix, WK, moves each one into a key.\nWhat question can this token help answer?\nTo score one pair, you take one token's query and another token's key and do the dot product.\nHigh value here means they're aligned.\nThis token has what the other one is looking for.\nQ_at_k transpose does every pair at once.\nThree tokens, a 3x3 grid of scores.\nThen divide by the square root of the head size, and softmax turns each row into weights\nthat add up to 1.\nTransformers process every position in parallel.\nAttention is how tokens decide who to pull information from.\nAnd attention scores measure which tokens are aligned under these Lerch projections."
}
